WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
The Hub is git for models.

2
00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:08.856
The Hugging Face Hub hosts three kinds of repositories: models, datasets, and Spaces (small hosted apps).

3
00:00:09.136 --> 00:00:20.037
Each repo is a git repository with large-file storage, owned by a user or an organization, so every file has a history and every version has a commit hash.

4
00:00:20.317 --> 00:00:25.160
That one fact shapes good practice: a model name like Qwen/Qwen3.

5
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:33.056
8-27B points at whatever is on the main branch today, while a commit hash points at exactly the files you tested.

6
00:00:33.336 --> 00:00:36.707
A model repo usually contains the weights (one or more.

7
00:00:36.987 --> 00:00:38.949
safetensors files), config.

8
00:00:39.229 --> 00:00:46.376
json (architecture, layer counts, context length), tokenizer files including the chat template, and a README.

9
00:00:46.656 --> 00:00:49.387
md that the Hub renders as the model card.

10
00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:59.608
Many popular models also have derivative repos uploaded by others: fine-tunes, quantized versions in GGUF or MLX format, and adapters.

11
00:00:59.888 --> 00:01:07.611
The Hub links them to their source through the base_model field, and you can browse a model’s quantizations and fine-tunes from its page.

12
00:01:07.891 --> 00:01:13.480
The Hugging Face LLM Course, which this lesson adapts, covers the Hub in its chapter 4.

13
00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:20.608
The short video below from that chapter shows the model page layout, the filters, and where the files and card live.
